# Repository conventions for coding agents

Copy this to `AGENTS.md` (or `CLAUDE.md`) at your repo root and edit. Most agent
harnesses read a root-level file of this name automatically. This is the
instruction half of mitigation M3 — moving files into `artifacts/` without this
file changes nothing, because the agent walks subdirectories too.

---

## Directory layout

| directory | agent should |
|---|---|
| `src/`, `tests/` | read and edit freely |
| `docs/` | read; edit when asked |
| `artifacts/` | **do not read.** Generated output. If you need to know what is in here, ask, or read the manifest at `artifacts/MANIFEST.md` instead |
| `data/raw/` | **do not read in full.** Sample with `head`/`pandas.read_csv(nrows=...)` |
| `.cache/`, `build/` | ignore entirely |

## Editing large files

Any file over ~20 KB — notebooks, generated JSON, fixtures — must be changed
with a **patch script**, not regenerated. Write the script to `patches/`, run
it, and keep it: it is the record of what changed and it is re-runnable if this
session ends.

Do not rewrite a notebook by rebuilding it from a generator. Load it, mutate
the specific cells, write it back.

## Notebooks

Notebooks in this repo are committed **without outputs**. Before editing one,
confirm it is stripped. Before committing, strip again:

```bash
jupyter nbconvert --clear-output --inplace path/to/nb.ipynb
```

## Verification

Run the whole check suite in one command and read the tail:

```bash
make check 2>&1 | tail -40
```

Do not run the linter, the type checker and the tests as three separate calls.

## Long tasks

At each natural boundary, update `STATE.md` with:

- what is done
- what is pending
- what was ruled out, and why (this is the part that is expensive to
  rediscover)

Keep it short enough that a fresh session can read it and continue without
replaying the conversation.

## Delegation

If you spawn a sub-agent, it must write results to disk incrementally. Work
that only exists in a sub-agent's context is lost if the session is
interrupted — not degraded, lost.
